; What V-0 must REFUSE, not mistranslate.
;
; `un bnot` — bitwise complement — is a VERIFIED-LEGAL module (`ssc3 check` says ok, `ssc3 exec`
; runs it) that the bridge has no case for, so the refusal it produces comes from the bridge and
; from nowhere else. That is the whole property this fixture holds: the emitter names what it
; cannot translate instead of emitting something plausible.
;
; THIS FIXTURE HAS NOW BEEN RE-POINTED TWICE, AND BOTH TIMES BECAUSE THE GATE WENT RED ON ITS OWN
; PROBE — which is the gate working, not failing.
;   - it held `globget` until 2026-08-04, when globals became translatable;
;   - it held `resume` until 2026-08-16, when effects did (`BridgeV2` §effects: `handle`, `perform`
;     and `resume` all translate now, and `v3/effects-gate.sh` runs all twelve effects fixtures on
;     both lanes).
; Re-point it the same way when the bridge grows a case for `un bnot`: find an instruction the
; emitter still has no arm for, check it verifies, and update `bridge-gate.sh`'s grep to the new
; name. When nothing is left to point at, that is worth saying out loud rather than deleting.
(module
  (consts (int 1))
  (types)
  (globals)
  (prims)
  (funcs
    (func "main" 0 2
      (const 1 0)
      (un bnot dyn 0 1)
      (ret 0)))
  (entry 0))
